 648 mil; 75/25 → ≈ 625 mil\" — matches my recalc. 632,305 might be old/alternate version (weighted on base amount rather than provisão). §6.1/§7 text may have both — need to check. 0.85×665,584+0.15×443,722.67=565,746.4+66,558.4=632,304.8 ✓ — so 632,305 is the weighting on exposicao (665,584) and 648,045 is on provisão. If the document cites both in different places with the same \"85/15\" label, it's a potential source of confusion but each might be contextually correct. Check actual text.\n\n- Monthly @12k 7,298.67: reflexos monthly @18k 10,948 → ×2/3 = 7,298.67 ✓. @18k 10,948: components/month: 13º 1,500 + férias+1/3 2,000 + FGTS 8%×(18,000+1,500+2,000)=1,720 + multa 40%×1,720=688 + INSS 28%×18,000=5,040 → 1,500+2,000+1,720+688+5,040=10,948 ✓. ×2/3=7,298.67 ✓.\n\n- HE extrapolável 160,159: extrapolate 135h/m ×54 months (Jan 2025–Sep 2026 = 9 months) to 58 months? 135×(58/6)?=1305h... calc: 16,568.18/6 = 2,761.36/m; ×58 = 160,159.1 ✓.\n\n- Perda esperada 660–755 mil: §8's calc: \"perda esperada ≈ R$ 660–755 mil mais correção... honorários\" — probably = probability-weighted with settlement/honorários: 0.70–0.80 × (943,581+ honorários?) hmm. 0.70×943,581=660,507 ✓; 0.80×943,581=754,865 ✓!! So expected loss 660–755k = 70–80% × worst case 943,581. ✓ (honorários separately \"mais... honorários\" — the text says \"perda esperada ≈ 660–755 mil mais correção ... e honorários\" — no issue.)\n\n- Worst case 943,581: check composition: 665,584 + 160,159 (extrapolated HE) + 117,838 = ? = 943,581 → 117,838 = ? INSS on 13º+férias (56,840) + ? 61,000? Hmm. Or 943,581 = 665,584 + 160,159 + 116,000 + 1,838? Odd. Or + 56,840 (INSS on 13º/férias) + 61,000? Let me look for §6's worst-case line. 943,581 − 825,743 = 117,838. 117,838 = 56,840 + 60,998? Hmm 60,998 ≈ ? Maybe multa 477 (18,000) + honorários (15% × 943,581 = 141,537)? Doesn't work. Need to read §6 to verify. Probably: worst = 665,584 + 56,840 (INSS 13º/férias) + 160,159 (HE) + 60,998?? No.\n\nAnother composition: 943,581 = 665,584 + 277,997; 277,997 = 160,159 + 117,838; 117,838 = INSS 28% on extrapolated HE? 28%×160,159=44,844.5 no. + multa 477 18,000 → 135,838? no.\n\nHmm — maybe férias double counting: férias 116,000 already in base; worst case adds \"férias em dobro\"? Art. 137: férias not granted within period → double payment: additional 116,000. 116,000 + something 1,838? Hmm 1,838? No.\n\nWait: 943,581 − 665,584 − 160,159 = 117,838. 117,838 = 56,840 + 60,998. 60,998? Strange. Or = 116,000 × 1.015836? Hmm. Or is worst case using corrected/updated HE? Anyway, let me read the section — this figure was in round 1's §6; round 1 review verified JSON totals but perhaps not this. If §6 itself shows a calculation that sums to 943,581, I'll trust the recalc. Let me verify with Python after reading.\n\nOther checks:\n- \"§8.2\" — item 2 reference.\n- §7.1 \"(§0/§3)\" — no issue.\n- §4.1 quote \"desde que ausente a subordinação\" — verify in clt file.\n- Theme 1.389 quote \"mérito pendente; suspensão mantida\" and \"a exposição não desaparece — fica em aberto, com juros e correção correndo\" — verify file's exact wording (confirmed in earlier truncation: \"**Situação nesta biblioteca (congelada em out/2026): mérito pendente; suspensão mantida.**\" ✓ and \"a exposição não desaparece — fica em aberto, com juros e correção correndo (Lei 14.905/2024: IPCA + SELIC-IPCA)\" ✓; \"qualquer informação que afirme tese definitiva sobre pejotização deve ser tratada como [não verificado]\" — need to verify this sentence exists (in earlier full-file reading? The tool result was truncated at \"Efeito prático:...\"). I quoted this as a warning in §4.1 — must verify.\n- \"notificação ... planilha de R$ 850 mil\" — verify in documents/.\n- INDEX status column: Súmulas 331/212/338/363, OJ 383 in force; cancelled 256, OJ 191 — deliverables should not cite these; grep \"256\" and \"191\" in deliverables.\n- JSON \"fundamentos\" — mentions of Súmula 338? Check if citations of OJ 383/331/363/212 are supported by library files.\n- Verify \"§8.2\" in parecer §7.1 body \"(§8.2)\" — §8 item 2 exists ✓.\n- Check STATUS \"nono fundamento\" ✓ (9 fundamentos).\n- Check header/claims in parecer.md line 5 etc.\n- Verify no other \"(§5)\" mis-reference exists elsewhere: grep all \"(§\" references in parecer.md and validate each.\n- Check §3 heading \"risco zero é erro\" etc., no issue.\n- Verify email notification date and amount in documents/notificacao_e_email_diretoria.txt.\n\nAdditionally: earlier \"632.305\" vs \"648.045\" — check §7's text: it says \"(85/15 → ≈ 648 mil; 75/25 → ≈ 625 mil)\". Where is 632,305? Perhaps §6.1 table has both exposicao-weighted and provisão-weighted. If §6.1 cites \"ponderado 85/15 ≈ 632 mil\" for exposicao and §7 says provisão 648 — both correct, no issue. Need to verify.\n\nAction plan:\n1. Read parecer.md in full (207 lines) — 1–2 reads.\n2. Read parecer.json in full.\n3. Read all 8 library files (small).\n4. grep deliverables for citations and cancelled súmulas; verify each citation against library.\n5. Python arithmetic re-verification for everything.\n6. Fix issues; enumerate changes.\n\nStart reads in parallel: parecer.md (1-110, 110-207), parecer.json, concatenation of library files (cat all 7 files in shell), documents/notificacao.\n","metadata":{"reasoningField":"reasoning"},"time":{"start":1792982960879,"end":1792982988814}}}
