.\" The +49 thousand claim: 13º/2021 (due 2021-12-20) and the vacation for vesting period 2020/10–2021/09 (due at the end of the concession period 2022-09-29) fall within the 5 years from the 2026-11-16 filing date? Hmm: 5 years before 2026-11-16 = 2021-11-16. Credit for 13º/2021 becomes due 2021-12-20 → after cutoff → claimable → +13º's 2021 portion (about 87,000/12×… hmm). Let me try computing what the +49 thousand is composed of: full-amount per due date: under that model, months from 2019-10 to 2021-11 might have salary already paid anyway; what additional items become claimable? 13º/2021 = 1/12… actually 13º/2021 is 18,000 (one full 13º salary) — under the conservative model the 58/12 already includes the 2021 portion for December. Hmm, the \"model\" difference: conservative approach = months of work from December 2021 onward (58 months). Per-due-date approach: 13º/2021 (due 2021-12-20, within 5 years from 2026-11-16) fully claimable — includes accrual for January–November 2021 (prescribed months). Under conservative model, the accrual-based 13º portion for January–November 2021 is lost. So the increment ≈ full 13º/2021 (18,000) minus the accrual portion already counted (December 2021 → 1/12×18,000=1,500) → +16,500? Plus vacation for vesting period 2020/10–2021/09 (due at the end of the concession period 2022-09-29 → claimable): vacation+1/3 = 24,000; under the conservative model, the accrual portion for the claimable months included in the 58/12… the accrual-based 58/12 method counts 58/12 of vacation ≈ 87,000 total; under the due-date model, the full 2020/10–2021/09 period (24,000) is added but its accrual is… this becomes complex; earlier I computed ≈ +49,000. From summary: \"model per due date ≈ +49,000.\" The composition should be re-verified. Let me reconstruct: plausible composition: 13º/2021 (11/12 of accrual outside the claimable window… hmm).\n\nLet me think carefully about how I got 49,000. Probably:\n- Full 13º/2021: 18,000. In the conservative model, December 2021 is included in the 58 months, giving 1/12 of accrual = 1,500 (in fact, 13º calculation 58/12×18,000 includes 1/12 for December 2021). Under the due-date model, the full 13º/2021 is due (vested in full by 2021-12-20, within 5 years from 2026-11-16). So increment = 18,000 − 1,500 = 16,500.\n- Vacation+1/3 for vesting period 2020/10–2021/09 (due 2022-09-29, within 5 years): full 24,000. Under the conservative accrual model, months of the vesting period after the cutoff: October–November 2021 prescribed; December 2021 is claimable and part of the vesting period 2021/10–2022/09 anyway. The conservative 58/12 vacation method includes 1/12 for December 2021 = 1,500+500 = 2,000 (including 1/3). Increment = 24,000 − 0? The vesting period 2020/10–2021/09 is entirely prescribed under the conservative model (all months October 2020–September 2021 < cutoff), so increment = +24,000.\n- FGTS/multa/INSS on the increment? FGTS on 13º and vacation: 8%×(16,500+24,000)=3,240; multa 40% → 1,296; INSS on 13º+vacation at 28% → 0.28×40,500=11,340. Total increment: 16,500+24,000+3,240+1,296+11,340 = 56,376. Hmm not 49,000.\n\nAlternative without INSS: 16,500+24,000+3,240+1,296 = 45,036 ≈ 45 thousand. Without multa+FGTS: 40,500. Hmm.\n\nMaybe my calculation was: 13º/2021 increment 16,500 + vacation 24,000 + FGTS/multa/INSS ≈ … 49,000? 16,500+24,000 = 40,500; +8%×40,500=3,240 → 43,740; +40%×3,240=1,296 → 45,036; ≈ +45 thousand, not 49.\n\nOr with INSS: 45,036 + 28%×40,500=11,340 → 56,376 ≈ +56 thousand.\n\nHmm. Neither is 49,000. Maybe I included FGTS on 13º/vacation differently, or included November 2021 (split month +10,948): 45,036+10,948 = 55,984? Not 49.\n\nAlternative composition: 13º/2021 full 18,000 + vacation 24,000 = 42,000; +FGTS 8%×42,000 = 3,360 → 45,360; +40% 1,344 → 46,704; hmm.\n\nOr: 18,000 (13º/2021 full, conservative model already includes 1,500 for December → but maybe counted in full 18,000, because under due-date model the full 13º/2021 is claimable, and