{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1792983299653,"sessionID":"ses_e89ef39bdffekVCoRunnygdKkc","part":{"id":"prt_17621ad6c001q5F4JpMh9vBhpw","sessionID":"ses_e89ef39bdffekVCoRunnygdKkc","messageID":"msg_17621a076001GjlQooOdfF3Rp6","type":"reasoning","text":"Alright, everything's assembled. STATUS item 3 and QUESTIONS Q3 correctly state ~160 hours vs. 135 hours (approx. 18%) — keep as is. The JSON's \"approx. R$19.600 unrecorded excess\" is misleading: the total derived from the daily average is ≈160 hours ≈ R$19.612, while the unrecorded portion is the difference ≈24.8 hours ≈ R$3.044. Fix the wording in the JSON.\n\nExact calculation: 159.8 × 122.72727 = 19.611.8. 24.8 × 122.72727 = 3.043.6.\n\nNow, apply the parecer.md edits. List:\n\n**Edit 1** (line 48): \"R$ 18.000 mensais certainos\" → \"R$ 18.000 mensais certos\".\n\n**Edit 2** (line 55): \"**Number of employees at Solaris not in file, see QUESTIONS; anyway, there exist attendance records in the claimant's possession**\" → \"**Number of employees at Solaris not in file, see QUESTIONS; in any case, the spreadsheet is in the company's own file — it's the presumption that doesn't apply (not the records), and the records themselves work against the company: 135 hours of recorded overtime**\".\n\nHmm, wording: Súmula 338 applies when the employer fails to submit records with 20+ employees. The point of this sentence: whether the presumption applies is unknown (employee count unknown), and anyway, since records exist in the company file, the Súmula 338 presumption has little to do with this case (records exist and show 135 hours). Draft: \"— **Number of employees at Solaris not in file, see QUESTIONS; anyway, the records exist in the company's own file, so the issue is the scope of the presumption, not the absence of records — which are unfavorable anyway (135 hours)**\". Shortened: \"— anyway, attendance records exist in the company's own file (presumption inapplicable due to non-absence; records are already unfavorable as is: 135 hours)\".\n\nSimpler and more accurate: \"**Number of employees at Solaris not in file, see QUESTIONS; anyway, attendance records exist in the company's own file — if the presumption applies, it would only reinforce the evidence already unfavorable in the records (135 hours of overtime)**\". Hmm. The original claimed the records were in the claimant's possession, but that's wrong (they're in the company file). The simplest correct version: \"anyway, attendance records exist in the company's own file, so there is no presumption of absent records — the hours already recorded in the spreadsheet (135 hours) work as is\". Going with this:\n\nOld: \"— **Number of employees at Solaris not in file, see QUESTIONS; anyway, there exist attendance records in the claimant's possession**.\"\nNew: \"— **Number of employees at Solaris not in file, see QUESTIONS**; in any case, attendance records exist in the company's own file, so there is no presumption of absent records — the 135 hours already recorded in the spreadsheet are evidence that exists as is.\"\n\n**Edit 3** (line 66): \"(licitude of intermediary work a distance, with autonomy)\" → \"(licitude of intermediary work à distância [at a distance], with autonomy)\".\n\n**Edit 4** (line 69): \"reliable estimate (§5)\" → \"reliable estimate (§6)\".\n\n**Edit 5** (line 78): \"**long suspensions** numerically **favor the claimant** (monetary update) and **favor immediate settlement** now (§6)\" → (§8).\n\n**Edit 6** (lines 85-86, §4.1 items 2-3):\n- Item 2: \"The file itself records that the thesis **does not negate recognition of an employment relationship when the requirements of CLT Article 3 and fraud (Article 9) are present**\" → insert \", in the concrete case,\" after \"when present\": \"...when present, in the concrete case, the requirements of CLT Article 3 and fraud (Article 9) are...\"\n- Item 3: Old: \"This is **in this task unverifiable — [unverified]** — and the file itself of Tema 1.389 warns that *'any information asserting the definitive thesis on pejotização [PJ exploitation] should be treated as [unverified]'*. Even in that hypothetical scenario\" → New: \"This is **in this task unverifiable — [unverified]** — the library is frozen in October 2026 and nothing in the file supports the existence of a judgment on the merits (methodological rule of this opinion: claims of a 'definitive thesis' outside the file are treated as **[unverified]**). Even in that hypothetical scenario\"\n- Also in item 3: \"(clauses 4–5, HR email, evaluation in CLT language, time-demand)\" → \"(clauses 4–5, HR-approved absences, evaluation in CLT language, time-demand)\".\n\n**Edit 7** (line 100): \"(13º salary/2021 matures 2021-12-20; vacation for the acquisition period Oct 2020–Sept 2021 matures at the end of the concession period 2022-09-29)\" → append a flag: \"(13º salary/2021 matures 2021-12-20; vacation for the acquisition period Oct 2020–Sept 2021 matures at the end of the concession period 2022-09-29 — maturity dates per general rules, **outside the library [unverified]**; the file gives only the 5-year cutoff from filing)\".\n\n**Edit 8** (line 120): \"hourly = 18,000/220 = 81.82; with 50% = 122.73; 135 h × 122.73\" → \"hourly = 18,000/220 = 81.8182; with 50% = 122.7273; 135 h × 122.7273\".\n\n**Edit 9** (line 126): \"135 × 122.73 = **R$ 16,568.18**\" → \"135 × 122.7273 = **R$ 16,568.18**\".\n**Edit 10** (line 127): \"1,305 h × 122.73 ≈ **R$ 160,159**\" → \"1,305 h × 122.7273 ≈ **R$ 160,159**\".\n**Edit 11** (line 129): \"FGTS+40% (2,210)\" → \"FGTS+40% (2,216)\".\n\n**Edit 12** (line 168): \"12,000/220 × 1.5 = 81.82/h × 135\" → \"12,000/220 × 1.5 = 81.8182/h × 135\". (Line 169: \"81.82 × 1,305\" → \"81.8182 × 1,305\".)\n\n**Edit 13** (line 173): Weighted mix. Old: \"Mix 85/15 → pay ≈ 0.85×665,584 + 0.15×443,722.67 = **632,305**; mix 75/25 → **610,119** (+ weighted proven overtime ≈ 15,188 → 625,306).\" New: \"Mix 85/15 → pay ≈ 0.85×665,584 + 0.15×443,722.67 = **632,305** + weighted overtime 0.85×16,568.18 + 0.15×11,045.45 ≈ 15,740 → **648,045**; mix 75/25 → **610,119** + weighted overtime ≈ 15,188 → **625,306**.\"\n\n**Edit 14** (line 186): \"(formula: `stf_tema_1389_pejotizacao.md` and `verbas_e_calculo.md`)\" → \"(formula in the library only in `stf_tema_1389_pejotizacao.md`)\".\n\n**Edit 15** (line 194): \"...why did the company, having received an extrajudicial notification with the R$850k spreadsheet and internal opinion, not book any provision?\" → \"...why did the company, having received an extrajudicial notification announcing the filing of a labor claim from 2019-10-01 'with all payments' (no amount attached) and an internal opinion estimating the liability, not book any provision?\"\n\n**Edit 16** (JSON line 28): new string: \"estimate: R$ 16,568.18 proven (135 h Jan–Jun 2025 × R$ 122.7273); extrapolable to ~R$ 160,159 for the 58 months claimable — to be examined; the average hours in the spreadsheet suggest ~160 h for the semester (≈ R$ 19,612), ~24.8 h (≈ R$ 3,044) above the 135 h recorded — variance not resolved\"\n\nAlso check other places: in STATUS/QUESTIONS, are there other places referencing \"R$19.600\" or \"850\"? None. STATUS mentions the 160h discrepancy — correct.\n\nCheck: §0 (line 16) — no problem. Line 128 — formula correct (verified); leave as is. But the wording is \"≈ **160 h** for the semester, **approx. 18% above**\" — no problem.\n\nWait, also confirm §6.1 label \"(updated round 2 — client confirms document absence)\" — per QUESTIONS (\"Q-A (newly added in round 2) — closed... response (2026-10-26, round 2)\"), correct. Keep.\n\nAlso, earlier checkpoint item: line 153 \"(round 2)\" — from §6.1 item 3: \"**Confirmed on 2026-10-26 (round 2)**: client states it holds **no additional information/documents whatsoever**\" — per QUESTIONS, correct (Q-A was asked in round 2, answered in round 2). Keep.\n\nOne more from checkpoint item 10: is the +49k verified? 44,500 × 1.112 = 49,484 ✓. Also \"add'l ≈ +R$49k\" 